 not the needed exponential or domain statement.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-additive-responses"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.additive_responses","kind":"claim","label":"Additive cut responses retain scalar second order","locator":"02-foundations.tex:1318–1449; cor:additive-response, eq:additive-response-parity, eq:additive-cut-response, eq:small-generator-error","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-foundations","statement":"For finite diagonal common-axis excluded Hamiltonians satisfying the explicit cut parity H(−a)=P H(a)P and polynomial time/input jet bounds, the cut difference has a first Gaussian-field response and a scalar second response. Replacements with small generator errors require, separately, smooth uniformity of their exponential families and lower responses.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.additive_responses","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.additive_responses","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.additive_responses%22%2C%22circuit.gate_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.additive_responses%22%2C%22circuit.gate_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.gate_calculus"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.helper_contraction","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.helper_contraction%22%2C%22circuit.additive_responses%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c0